  <title>Mouse review and clicking</title>
  <p>
    Mouse review presents accessible objects under the mouse pointer as you move it. Unlike flat
    review, it is not limited to the active window.
  </p>
  <p>
    Orca also provides pointer-routing and clicking commands. Mouse review, pointer routing, and
    simulated clicks may not work as expected, or at all, on Wayland. Accessible actions can
    still work when supported by the application or toolkit.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-mouse-review-and-clicking">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Mouse</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present tooltips</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca presents tooltips that appear when the pointer hovers over an object. Tooltips
          requested from the keyboard, such as with Ctrl+F1 in supported applications, are
          presented regardless of this setting. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak object under mouse</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca speaks the object under the mouse pointer as the pointer moves. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-mouse">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Mouse</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Perform left click on current item</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Keypad Divide</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>7</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Acts on the flat review location when flat review is active, or on the focused object
          otherwise. Orca first tries suitable accessible actions exposed by the object through
          its application or toolkit. If no suitable action succeeds, Orca tries to simulate a
          mouse click at the object's location. Simulated clicks do not currently work on
          Wayland.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Perform right click on current item</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Keypad Multiply</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>8</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Acts on the flat review location when flat review is active, or on the focused object
          otherwise. Orca first tries suitable accessible actions exposed by the object through
          its application or toolkit. If no suitable action succeeds, Orca tries to simulate a
          mouse click at the object's location. Simulated clicks do not currently work on
          Wayland.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Route the pointer to the current item</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Keypad Divide</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>9</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Routes the pointer to the flat review location when flat review is active, or to the
          focused object otherwise.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle mouse review mode</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Turns mouse review on or off for the current session, whether or not it is enabled in
          preferences.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
